; print writes a cost with the decimals the journal gave it.  The zeros
; are part of the cost's precision: an amount inferred from a cost is
; shown to the cost's decimals (#1151), so a printed journal that drops
; them reports a different balance (`ledger generate` seeds 9, 15 and 16
; failed their print round trip this way).  A cost never teaches its
; commodity a precision, so of these only EUR, written as an amount,
; has one.  A cost given by an expression has the precision its
; evaluation gives it, and a division adds digits: `@ (10.50 N / 2)`
; prints as `@ N5.25000000`, which the inferred amount N-15.75000000 is
; shown to.

